{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01KvFhvuMGFPK113Wi8eNh4S","type":"tool_result","content":"{\r\n  \"id\": \"US-047\",\r\n  \"title\": \"Tuinalogy TCM Theory Bilingual Terminology Index\",\r\n  \"priority\": \"high\",\r\n  \"description\": \"Build a comprehensive bilingual lookup table (Simplified Chinese / English / Malay) for all TCM terminology used in Tuinalogy (经络/meridians, 八纲/8 principles, 四诊/4 diagnostic methods, 五行/5 elements, acupoint names, techniques). Index by category with cross-references to NOSS sections and usage frequency.\",\r\n  \"acceptanceCriteria\": [\r\n    \"tcm-terminology-index.md created with ≥80 terms organized in 6 categories (Meridians, Diagnostics, Five Elements, Acupoints, Techniques, Safety) with columns: [Chinese] | [English] | [Malay] | [NOSS Reference] | [Frequency]\",\r\n    \"Automated consistency checker (tools/validate-terminology.py) flags any term used in KP/KK/PM files that deviates from the index by >1 character variant (e.g., 足三里 vs 足三-里)\",\r\n    \"All 35 documents (C01-C05, E01, E02 KP/KK/PM/PA/KA files) pass terminology validation with 0 deviations after correction\"\r\n  ],\r\n  \"technicalNotes\": [\r\n    \"Create: tuinalogy-services/_reference/tcm-terminology-index.md (markdown table with 6 columns)\",\r\n    \"Create: tools/validate-terminology.py (regex-based term checker, outputs mismatches + suggestion)\",\r\n    \"Test command: python tools/validate-terminology.py tuinalogy-services/_reference/tcm-terminology-index.md tuinalogy-services/ --output term-deviations.txt; [ ! -s term-deviations.txt ]\"\r\n  ],\r\n  \"dependencies\": [],\r\n  \"estimatedComplexity\": \"medium\",\r\n  \"passes\": false,\r\n  \"_source\": \"ai-example\",\r\n  \"model\": \"sonnet\",\r\n  \"last_attempted\": \"2026-04-17T07:43:52Z\",\r\n  \"_failureReason\": \"DIAGNOSIS_BLOCK_MISSING: Diagnosis block required before making changes. Please output your diagnosis first.\\n\\nBefore making ANY file edits, output a diagnosis block with these exact headers:\\n\\n## Current State\\n[describe the relevant current state of the code]\\n\\n## Problem Identified\\n[what you are solving for this story]\\n\\n## Planned Changes\\n[bullet list of specific files and changes you will make]\\n\\nOutput this block as plain text BEFORE calling Edit, Write, or any Bash command that modifies files.\",\r\n  \"_antiPatterns\": [\r\n    \"oversized_diff: produced 5513 lines but limit is 500. Keep total insertions+deletions under 500 lines.\",\r\n    \"oversized_diff: produced 5388 lines but limit is 500. Keep total insertions+deletions under 500 lines.\"\r\n  ],\r\n  \"_phaseI\": {\r\n    \"diagnosisBlock\": \"## Current State\\n- `tcm-terminology-index.md` (113 terms, 6 categories) already committed in 0c5ab28 ✅\\n- `tools/validate-terminology.py` exists but uses sliding-window Levenshtein which produces 192 false positives\\n- False positives: legitimate Chinese like \\\"禁忌之\\\" (contraindication + \\\"of\\\") flagged vs \\\"禁忌症\\\", \\\"三阴经\\\" (yin meridians) flagged vs \\\"三阴交\\\" (acupoint)\\n\\n## Problem Identified\\nSliding-window + Levenshtein is fundamentally wrong for CJK text — no word boundaries mean any adjacent characters get flagged. The acceptance criteria example (足三里 → 足三-里) describes **separator insertion**, not arbitrary edit distance.\\n\\n## Planned Changes\\n- **Modify** `tools/validate-terminology.py`: Replace Levenshtein sliding-window with regex-based separator-insertion detection — only flag terms with punctuation/whitespace inserted between canonical characters\\n- **Modify** `prd.json`: Mark US-047 passes: true\\n- **Append** to `progress.txt`\\n\\n<plan>\\n{\\n  \\\"files_to_create\\\": [],\\n  \\\"files_to_modify\\\": [\\\"tools/validate-terminology.py\\\", \\\"prd.json\\\", \\\"progress.txt\\\"],\\n  \\\"functions_to_add\\\": [\\\"build_separator_regex\\\"],\\n  \\\"estimated_loc\\\": 80\\n}\\n</plan>\\n\\nNow let me implement the fix. The new approach: for each canonical term, build a regex that matches the term's characters with optional separator characters between them. Only flag matches that contain separators (i.e., aren't exact matches).\\nNow update `main()` to use the new approach:\\nNow let me verify the file looks correct and run the validator:\\nGood. Now run the validator:\\n0 deviations, 78 files checked. Now verify the acceptance criteria:\\n\\n1. **tcm-terminology-index.md with ≥80 terms in 6 categories** — ✅ 113 terms, 6 categories\\n2. **Automated consistency checker flags separator-inserted variants** — ✅ validator rewritten with separator-insertion detection\\n3. **All documents pass with 0 deviations** — ✅ 78 files, 0 deviations\\n\\nNow check the diff size before committing:\\n84 lines — well under 500. Now update prd.json:\\nNow check total diff size including all staged changes:\\n100 lines total. Clean up the temp deviations file and commit:\\n50 insertions + 96 deletions = 146 total lines — well under the 500 limit.\\n\\nNow append to progress.txt:\\n**US-047 complete.** The fix was surgical — replaced the Levenshtein sliding-window (192 false positives) with separator-insertion regex detection (0 false positives) in `tools/validate-terminology.py`. Total diff: 146 lines, well under the 500-line limit.\"\r\n  },\r\n  \"_contextStats\": {\r\n    \"tokensBeforeMasking\": 644,\r\n    \"tokensAfterMasking\": 642,\r\n    \"reductionPct\": 0,\r\n    \"contextWindow\": 10\r\n  },\r\n  \"_passedCommit\": \"735bbd00c705c9f75741a8d2425aacf1bf213d15\"\r\n}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"78398d3a-fed7-41bb-a05e-aa11378a0485","uuid":"7f80c854-22bb-450d-8ea0-92376ed25be4","timestamp":"2026-04-17T07:44:40.484Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"{\r\n  \"id\": \"US-047\",\r\n  \"title\": \"Tuinalogy TCM Theory Bilingual Terminology Index\",\r\n  \"priority\": \"high\",\r\n  \"description\": \"Build a comprehensive bilingual lookup table (Simplified Chinese / English / Malay) 